TI  - MolCompass: multi-tool for the navigation in chemical space and visual validation 
      of QSAR/QSPR models.
PG  - 98
LID - 10.1186/s13321-024-00888-z [doi]
LID - 98
AB  - The exponential growth of data is challenging for humans because their ability to 
      analyze data is limited. Especially in chemistry, there is a demand for tools 
      that can visualize molecular datasets in a convenient graphical way. We propose a 
      new, ready-to-use, multi-tool, and open-source framework for visualizing and 
      navigating chemical space. This framework adheres to the low-code/no-code (LCNC) 
      paradigm, providing a KNIME node, a web-based tool, and a Python package, making 
      it accessible to a broad cheminformatics community. The core technique of the 
      MolCompass framework employs a pre-trained parametric t-SNE model. We demonstrate 
      how this framework can be adapted for the visualisation of chemical space and 
      visual validation of binary classification QSAR/QSPR models, revealing their 
      weaknesses and identifying model cliffs. All parts of the framework are publicly 
      available on GitHub, providing accessibility to the broad scientific community. 
      Scientific contributionWe provide an open-source, ready-to-use set of tools for 
      the visualization of chemical space. These tools can be insightful for chemists 
      to analyze compound datasets and for the visual validation of QSAR/QSPR models.
