TI  - PUResNetV2.0: a deep learning model leveraging sparse representation for improved 
      ligand binding site prediction.
PG  - 66
LID - 10.1186/s13321-024-00865-6 [doi]
LID - 66
AB  - Accurate ligand binding site prediction (LBSP) within proteins is essential for 
      drug discovery. We developed ProteinUNetResNetV2.0 (PUResNetV2.0), leveraging 
      sparse representation of protein structures to improve LBSP accuracy. Our 
      training dataset included protein complexes from 4729 protein families. 
      Evaluations on benchmark datasets showed that PUResNetV2.0 achieved an 85.4% 
      Distance Center Atom (DCA) success rate and a 74.7% F1 Score on the Holo801 
      dataset, outperforming existing methods. However, its performance in specific 
      cases, such as RNA, DNA, peptide-like ligand, and ion binding site prediction, 
      was limited due to constraints in our training data. Our findings underscore the 
      potential of sparse representation in LBSP, especially for oligomeric structures, 
      suggesting PUResNetV2.0 as a promising tool for computational drug discovery.
