TI  - IntelliPatent: a web-based intelligent system for fast chemical patent claim 
      drafting.
PG  - 78
LID - 10.1186/s13321-019-0401-4 [doi]
LID - 78
AB  - The first step of automating composition patent drafting is to draft the claims 
      around a Markush structure with substituents. Currently, this process depends 
      heavily on experienced attorneys or patent agents, and few tools are available. 
      IntelliPatent was created to accelerate this process. Users can simply upload a 
      series of analogs of interest, and IntelliPatent will automatically extract the 
      general structural scaffold and generate the patent claim text. The program can 
      also extend the patent claim by adding commonly seen R groups from historical 
      lists of the top 30 selling drugs in the US for all R substituents. The program 
      takes MDL SD file formats as inputs, and the invariable core structure and 
      variable substructures will be identified as the initial scaffold and R groups in 
      the output Markush structure. The results can be downloaded in MS Word format 
      (.docx). The suggested claims can be quickly generated with IntelliPatent. This 
      web-based tool is freely accessible at https://intellipatent.cmdm.tw/.
