TI  - A retrosynthetic analysis algorithm implementation.
PG  - 1
LID - 10.1186/s13321-018-0323-6 [doi]
LID - 1
AB  - The need for synthetic route design arises frequently in discovery-oriented 
      chemistry organizations. While traditionally finding solutions to this problem 
      has been the domain of human experts, several computational approaches, aided by 
      the algorithmic advances and the availability of large reaction collections, have 
      recently been reported. Herein we present our own implementation of a 
      retrosynthetic analysis method and demonstrate its capabilities in an attempt to 
      identify synthetic routes for a collection of approved drugs. Our results 
      indicate that the method, leveraging on reaction transformation rules learned 
      from a large patent reaction dataset, can identify multiple theoretically 
      feasible synthetic routes and, thus, support research chemist everyday efforts.
