TI  - Modeling enzyme-ligand binding in drug discovery.
PG  - 48
LID - 48
AB  - Enzymes are one of the most important groups of drug targets, and identifying 
      possible ligand-enzyme interactions is of major importance in many drug discovery 
      processes. Novel computational methods have been developed that can apply the 
      information from the increasing number of resolved and available ligand-enzyme 
      complexes to model new unknown interactions and therefore contribute to answer 
      open questions in the field of drug discovery like the identification of unknown 
      protein functions, off-target binding, ligand 3D homology modeling and 
      induced-fit simulations.
