TI  - A machine learning platform for the discovery of materials.
PG  - 42
LID - 10.1186/s13321-021-00518-y [doi]
LID - 42
AB  - For photovoltaic materials, properties such as band gap [Formula: see text] are 
      critical indicators of the material's suitability to perform a desired function. 
      Calculating [Formula: see text] is often performed using Density Functional 
      Theory (DFT) methods, although more accurate calculation are performed using 
      methods such as the GW approximation. DFT software often used to compute 
      electronic properties includes applications such as VASP, CRYSTAL, CASTEP or 
      Quantum Espresso. Depending on the unit cell size and symmetry of the material, 
      these calculations can be computationally expensive. In this study, we present a 
      new machine learning platform for the accurate prediction of properties such as 
      [Formula: see text] of a wide range of materials.
