TI  - A path to next-generation reproducibility in cheminformatics.
PG  - 62
LID - 10.1186/s13321-019-0385-0 [doi]
LID - 62
AB  - Currently, the submission guidelines for the Journal of Cheminformatics say it 
      will "only publish research or software that is entirely reproducible by third 
      parties." They go on to specify that being reproducible means that anything 
      essential to the conclusion of the paper be freely accessible and states that 
      source code must be provided. I submit that this definition of reproducibility is 
      too narrow-that a cheminformatics method can only truly be replicated by 
      reimplementing it from a detailed, step-by-step high-level description to 
      determine how reliably the algorithm per se does what it is intended to do.
