TI  - PUG-View: programmatic access to chemical annotations integrated in PubChem.
PG  - 56
LID - 10.1186/s13321-019-0375-2 [doi]
LID - 56
AB  - PubChem is a chemical data repository that provides comprehensive information on 
      various chemical entities. It contains a wealth of chemical information from 
      hundreds of data sources. Programmatic access to this large amount of data 
      provides researchers with new opportunities for data-intensive research. PubChem 
      provides several programmatic access routes. One of these is PUG-View, which is a 
      Representational State Transfer (REST)-style web service interface specialized 
      for accessing annotation data contained in PubChem. The present paper describes 
      various aspects of PUG-View, including the scope of data accessible through 
      PUG-View, the syntax for formulating a PUG-View request URL, the difference of 
      PUG-View from other web service interfaces in PubChem, and its limitations and 
      usage policies.
