TI  - Two inhibitors of yeast plasma membrane ATPase 1 (ScPma1p): toward the 
      development of novel antifungal therapies.
PG  - 6
LID - 10.1186/s13321-018-0261-3 [doi]
LID - 6
AB  - Given that many antifungal medications are susceptible to evolved resistance, 
      there is a need for novel drugs with unique mechanisms of action. Inhibiting the 
      essential proton pump Pma1p, a P-type ATPase, is a potentially effective 
      therapeutic approach that is orthogonal to existing treatments. We identify 
      NSC11668 and hitachimycin as structurally distinct antifungals that inhibit yeast 
      ScPma1p. These compounds provide new opportunities for drug discovery aimed at 
      this important target.
